From: MYIR BSP <support@myir.com>
Subject: [PATCH] board: myd_jmx95: link current NXP MMC and TCPC helpers

SYS_VENDOR is myir, so the top-level Makefile does not automatically build
board/nxp/common. Include it explicitly, following verdin-imx95, to resolve
the board's MMC environment and USB Type-C calls without copying old APIs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MYIR board integration]

--- a/board/myir/myd_jmx95/Makefile
+++ b/board/myir/myd_jmx95/Makefile
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #
 
 obj-y += myd_jmx95.o
+obj-y += ../../nxp/common/
 
 ifdef CONFIG_SPL_BUILD
 obj-y += spl.o
